{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated [client.py](/workspace/in/schema_migration/client.py) to handle the full migration contract instead of the stub.\n\nIt now converts legacy `v1`, `v1.1`, and `v1.2` payloads into the v2 shape, supports already-v2 payloads idempotently, defaults blank/null shipping methods to `\"standard\"`, preserves allowed unknown fields under `metadata.unknownFields`, drops obvious PII-like extras, aggregates batch errors and warnings via `convert_many`, writes [conversion_audit.json](/workspace/in/schema_migration/conversion_audit.json), and adds `python -m client input.jsonl output.json` JSONL-to-JSON CLI support.\n\nI could not run `python -m pytest` exactly here because this environment has no `python` executable and no `pytest` installed under `python3`. I did verify the visible cases and sample payloads with targeted `python3` runs; the converter produced the expected v2 records, useful error paths like `customer_id`, and an audit summary with converted/error/warning/PII/unknown-field counts."}}
